.TH WPRINTIDLE-C 1 "2026-01-01" "wprintidle-c" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wprintidle-c \- Query idle time from Wayland idle time monitor daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wprintidle-c
.RI [ -s | --seconds ]
.RI [ -m | --milliseconds ]
.RI [ -h | --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wprintidle-c
is a client program that queries the current user idle time from the
.B wprintidle-c-daemon
background service. The daemon monitors idle state on Wayland compositors that
support the
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
protocol.
.PP
The idle time represents how long the user has been inactive (no keyboard or
mouse activity). The client connects to the daemon via a Unix domain socket,
retrieves the current idle time, prints it to standard output, and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -s ", " --seconds
Print idle time in seconds. This is the default behavior.
.TP
.BR -m ", " --milliseconds
Print idle time in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display help message and exit.
.SH USAGE
Before using the client, ensure the daemon is running (see DAEMON section below).
.PP
Query idle time in seconds (default):
.PP
.nf
.RS
wprintidle-c
.RE
.fi
.PP
Query idle time in milliseconds:
.PP
.nf
.RS
wprintidle-c -m
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use in shell scripts:
.PP
.nf
.RS
if [ $(wprintidle-c) -gt 300 ]; then
    echo "Idle for more than 5 minutes"
fi
.RE
.fi
.SH DAEMON
The
.B wprintidle-c-daemon
service must be running before you can query idle time.
.SS Starting the Daemon
Start the daemon using systemd (recommended):
.PP
.nf
.RS
systemctl --user enable wprintidle-c.service --now
.RE
.fi
.PP
Or start manually with custom timeout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
wprintidle-c-daemon [timeout_ms] &
.RE
.fi
.PP
The
.I timeout_ms
parameter (default: 1000) specifies how long in milliseconds before the user is
considered idle.
.SS Daemon Communication
The daemon listens on a Unix domain socket at
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wprintidle-c.sock .
The client communicates with the daemon through this socket.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.B wprintidle-c
requires:
.IP \(bu 2
A Wayland compositor
.IP \(bu 2
Compositor support for the
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
protocol
.PP
The program will exit with an error if these requirements are not met.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successfully retrieved and printed idle time
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred (daemon not running, invalid arguments, or connection failed)
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic Idle Time Query
Query current idle time in seconds:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ wprintidle-c
5
.RE
.fi
.SS Emacs org-mode Integration
Configure Emacs org-mode to use wprintidle-c for idle detection:
.PP
.nf
.RS
(setq org-clock-x11idle-program-name "wprintidle-c")
.RE
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If the client reports that the daemon is not running, verify the daemon status:
.PP
.nf
.RS
systemctl --user status wprintidle-c.service
.RE
.fi
.PP
Check if the socket exists:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ls -l $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wprintidle-c.sock
.RE
.fi
.PP
View daemon logs:
.PP
.nf
.RS
journalctl --user -u wprintidle-c.service -f
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wprintidle-c-daemon ,
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Wayland protocol extension:
.I ext-idle-notify-v1
